// Preview only: King Kong's CRO page, rebuilt in Brandon's voice around the lead-to-customer path.
import KkShell from '../../components/KkShell.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is conversion rate optimization?', a: "Getting more of the people who already found you to become customers. Say 1,000 people visit your site in a month and 10 fill out the form. That's a 1% conversion rate. Getting it to 2% doubles your leads without spending another dollar on ads. For a business with a phone, it also means getting more of those leads to book, and more of the booked to pay." },
  { q: 'What is a good conversion rate?', a: "Above 2% on a page is decent. Above 5% is great. Some of the best landing pages we've run convert at 20% or more. But the number that matters more for most of our clients is how many leads become booked jobs, and that one is almost always fixable fast, because it's usually about speed." },
  { q: 'Do I have a traffic problem or a conversion problem?', a: "Nearly always conversion. You can buy more traffic any day of the week. If the leads you already get are sitting in an inbox for four hours, more traffic just means more leads sitting in an inbox. Fix the path first, then turn up the ads." },
  { q: 'How much does it cost?', a: "It depends on how many pages and steps we need to look at and test. Sometimes it's a one-time project, sometimes ongoing. For our Demand Flow clients it's built in, because we don't send ads to a path that leaks." },
  { q: 'Does conversion affect SEO?', a: "Yes. When people stay on your site, call, and don't bounce straight back to Google, that's a signal Google reads as a good result. Better pages rank better over time." },
  { q: 'What conversion rate can I expect?', a: "On an existing campaign we aim to beat what you've got by a wide margin. On a new one we aim for at least 3% on the page and a lot more on the phone. On a call we look at your actual numbers before anybody promises anything." },
];
---

<KkShell
  title="Conversion Rate Optimization (Preview)"
  description="More customers from the traffic you already have, in the Dead River look."
  kicker="CONVERSION"
  headline="MORE CUSTOMERS FROM THE PEOPLE WHO ALREADY FOUND YOU. WITHOUT SPENDING ANOTHER DOLLAR ON ADS."
  sub="Most businesses don't have a traffic problem. They have a leak between the click and the paid job."
  faqTitle="CONVERSION, STRAIGHT ANSWERS"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="kk-dear">Hey,</p>
  <p>Let me ask you something. What's stopping you from doubling your ad spend tomorrow?</p>
  <p>You want more customers. Google and Facebook will sell you all the traffic you can afford. So why not just buy it?</p>
  <p>My guess is you already know the answer. Because the leads you get now don't all turn into jobs, and twice the leads would just mean twice the leak.</p>
  <p>So let's be honest. A lack of traffic isn't what's holding you back. The path from the click to the paid job is.</p>
  <p>Here's where we see it leak, in order, from pulling the last ten leads with a lot of owners.</p>
  <h2>LEAK ONE: NOBODY SAW THE OFFER</h2>
  <p>Out of 100 people who see an ad, only two or three click. If the ad looks like an ad, with a logo and a stock photo and "quality service you can trust," most people scroll right past, and you never get the chance to sell them anything. The ad's only job is the click. A real photo and a headline that says one specific thing fixes more of this than any setting in the account.</p>
  <h2>LEAK TWO: THE PAGE DIDN'T MATCH</h2>
  <p>They clicked an ad about water heaters and landed on your home page. Now they're looking at a menu, a mission statement, and a photo of your truck. They leave. The page has to say the same thing the ad said, in the same words, with the next step right there. Half of the clicks you pay for die on this one.</p>
  <h2>LEAK THREE: NOBODY CALLED BACK IN FIVE MINUTES</h2>
  <p>This is the big one, and the cheapest to fix. A lead that gets a call back in 5 minutes books. A lead that gets a call back tomorrow already hired the other guy. We've watched businesses double their booked jobs from the exact same ad spend by doing nothing except answering faster. A phone alert instead of an inbox. A person, not an auto-reply. It's written into our guarantee because it's the biggest lever there is.</p>
  <h2>LEAK FOUR: THEY DIDN'T BELIEVE YOU</h2>
  <p>People are tired. They've heard every promise. If your page says "best in town" and nothing else, they don't believe it, and they shouldn't. Show, don't tell. Real reviews with names. Real before and after photos. The real number of jobs you've done. A guarantee you'll actually honor. We put $50,000 in writing because it's the most believable thing we can say.</p>
  <h2>LEAK FIVE: THE QUOTE DIED IN AN INBOX</h2>
  <p>You sent the quote and never heard back. Most quotes don't lose to a competitor. They lose to silence. "When do you want to go over it?" written down as a task with a name on it, and a follow-up on that date. That's the whole trick.</p>
  <h2>HERE'S THE MATH</h2>
  <p>Say you sell a $3,000 job and spend $3,000 a month on ads for 100 leads. If 1 in 10 books, that's 10 jobs, $30,000. If the five fixes above get you to 2 in 10, same ads, same leads, that's $60,000. Nothing changed except the path.</p>
  <p>That's why we fix the path before we turn up the ads, and why our guarantee is on revenue, not clicks.</p>
  <p class="kk-ps">P.S. Part 1 of Marketing is F*cking Easy is the whole lead-to-customer path, step by step, with the scripts and the checklists. Free, further down. The 5-minute page alone is worth the download.</p>
</KkShell>
